[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
LiveKit Egress has been installed as %%PREFIX%%/bin/livekit-egress.

1. Redis. Egress takes its requests from the LiveKit server over Redis, so
   it must use the same Redis as the server (redis: in livekit.yaml). Redis
   can run on another host and is therefore not a package dependency; for a
   local one install databases/redis and enable it.

2. Configure:
     cp %%ETCDIR%%/egress.yaml.sample %%ETCDIR%%/egress.yaml
   and set api_key, api_secret, ws_url and redis.

3. Enable and start:
     sysrc livekit_egress_enable=YES
     service livekit_egress start
   Output goes to /var/log/livekit_egress.log. "service livekit_egress stop"
   ends running egresses and uploads them; set livekit_egress_sig_stop=TERM
   to wait for them to finish instead.

Local file outputs (no storage: upload configured) are written by the
%%LIVEKIT_EGRESS_USER%% user: request absolute paths it can write to, for
example below %%LIVEKIT_EGRESS_HOME%%. Work files and IPC sockets live in
%%LIVEKIT_EGRESS_HOME%%/tmp, which is emptied on every start.
EOM
}
%%CHROME_MSG%%{ type: install
%%CHROME_MSG%%  message: <<EOM
%%CHROME_MSG%%Room composite and web egress (CHROME option):
%%CHROME_MSG%%
%%CHROME_MSG%%- The rc.d script starts a private PulseAudio daemon as %%LIVEKIT_EGRESS_USER%%
%%CHROME_MSG%%  (socket in /var/run/livekit_egress/xdg, settings in
%%CHROME_MSG%%  %%DATADIR%%/pulse) and stops it with the service.
%%CHROME_MSG%%- Every such egress starts its own Xvfb display; its socket lives in
%%CHROME_MSG%%  /tmp/.X11-unix and, as upstream, it runs without X access control, so
%%CHROME_MSG%%  local users can connect to it. Run egress on a host or jail without
%%CHROME_MSG%%  untrusted local users.
%%CHROME_MSG%%- Chrome must play audio through PulseAudio. www/chromium does so with its
%%CHROME_MSG%%  PULSEAUDIO option (on by default); a chromium built with only SNDIO or
%%CHROME_MSG%%  ALSA produces recordings without sound.
%%CHROME_MSG%%- In a jail, give it SysV shared memory (sysvshm=new) for the X server's
%%CHROME_MSG%%  MIT-SHM extension.
%%CHROME_MSG%%EOM
%%CHROME_MSG%%}
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%{ type: install
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%  message: <<EOM
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%Built without the CHROME option, so there is no Chromium, Xvfb or
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%PulseAudio. Track, track composite and participant egress work; room
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%composite works through the GStreamer compositor with the built-in
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%layouts (enable_template_sdk: true, which egress.yaml.sample sets, as
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%well as pulse_sink_reap_grace_sec: -1). Web egress and custom
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%templates need the CHROME option.
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%EOM
%%NO_CHROME_MSG%%}
]
